assertion  XSH.2.9-threads.022
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.9.5.2
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      2001
says       As XSH.2.9-threads.012, for msgsnd() and msgrcv() with IPC_NOWAIT.
note       The assertion rests on the sentence that a call to a cancellation
           point acts on a request already made before it returns. The functions
           are called with arguments that let them finish at once, so a function
           that returns has not acted on the request; side effects of the call
           are not checked (they are those of a call interrupted by a signal). A
           function that blocks despite the request is caught by a 5 s wait and
